I have successfully found and extracted the 'Welcome to SuperNorm - Onboarding Tips' from within the Bland AI product console. This content provides a good overview of how to get started with building AI voice agents.

(1) What I accomplished: I found in-product onboarding tips for Bland AI, specifically 'Welcome to SuperNorm - Onboarding Tips'.

(2) Things I LIKED about Bland AI's UX for this goal:
    - The 'How may I help?' chat feature, while not directly providing the onboarding tips I was looking for, is a good attempt at in-product support.
    - The onboarding tips themselves are well-structured and easy to understand, covering core concepts, a good first session, building pathways, testing & debugging, analytics, and good habits.
    - The console is generally clean and well-organized, making it relatively easy to navigate.

(3) Things I DISLIKED or found confusing:
    - The 'Docs' and 'Bland University' links in the sidebar lead to external websites, which is not ideal for in-product help/onboarding. It would be better if these were integrated or clearly labeled as external.
    - The 'How may I help?' chat feature did not provide a direct link to the onboarding tips when I typed 'onboarding tips'. It would be more helpful if it could surface relevant in-product content.
    - The 'Account / Settings / Organization' hint was not directly useful in finding onboarding tips, and I had to scroll extensively to confirm this.

(4) How hard this felt: Medium. While the onboarding tips were eventually found, it required exploring multiple avenues and scrolling, as the initial attempts to find in-product help led to external documentation or an unhelpful chat response.


