I successfully found in-product help/docs/onboarding entry through the 'Conductor' chat feature. The chat provided links to full documentation (https://docs.retellai.com), support email (support@retellai.com), and a community forum (https://community.retellai.com/c/support-help/6). It also mentioned specific sections like 'Getting started' (docs/get-started/) and 'General platform overview' (docs/general/).

**Things I LIKED about Retell AI's UX for this goal:**
1. The 'Conductor' chat feature is an excellent, interactive way to get help and find documentation. It's very intuitive and provides direct links.
2. The 'Getting started' button on the main dashboard is a clear entry point for new users.
3. The documentation seems comprehensive, covering various aspects from building to deploying and testing agents.

**Things I DISLIKED or found confusing:**
1. The sidebar icons were not immediately clear for help/docs. The 'i' icon led to billing, which was misleading.
2. There wasn't an obvious 'Help' or 'Docs' link directly in the main navigation or sidebar, requiring exploration or the use of the chat feature.
3. The repeated scrolling of the sidebar was unproductive as it didn't reveal new elements, indicating a potential UI issue or lack of clear visual cues for more content.

**How hard this felt:** Medium. While the 'Conductor' chat was very effective once found, the initial exploration of the sidebar and misdirection to the billing page added some complexity. If the 'Conductor' chat wasn't available, finding the documentation would have been harder.


